WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.932
At this point you may be wondering

00:00:01.945 --> 00:00:03.366
when you should use a function a

00:00:03.392 --> 00:00:06.526
dictionary or a class There is no

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.079
need to use a class for every

00:00:08.092 --> 00:00:11.618
problem In fact the simplest structure that

00:00:11.645 --> 00:00:13.724
clearly solves the problem is usually the

00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:16.540
best choice Use a function when you

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:19.118
mainly need to perform one reusable task

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.382
For example a function called get profit

00:00:22.408 --> 00:00:24.526
can receive sales and costs and return

00:00:24.553 --> 00:00:27.355
the profit Use a dictionary when you

00:00:27.382 --> 00:00:30.645
mainly need to store related values For

00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:33.026
example a product dictionary might store a

00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:36.592
product name price and category Use a

00:00:36.605 --> 00:00:38.500
class when the data and the behavior

00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:42.395
naturally belong together For example a Product

00:00:42.421 --> 00:00:44.053
class can store a name and price

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:46.092
and also provide a sale price method

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.816
A class is especially useful when you

00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:50.711
expect to create many objects of the

00:00:50.724 --> 00:00:52.658
same type or when several methods need

00:00:52.671 --> 00:00:54.342
to work with the same stored data

00:00:55.276 --> 00:00:57.382
But classes also add structure so do

00:00:57.395 --> 00:00:59.184
not use them simply because they look

00:00:59.197 --> 00:01:02.237
more advanced A good beginner rule is

00:01:02.263 --> 00:01:04.987
to start simple If a function is

00:01:05.013 --> 00:01:08.105
enough use a function If you only

00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:10.658
need to store related values a dictionary

00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:13.342
may be enough Move to a class

00:01:13.368 --> 00:01:15.579
when one concept clearly has both stored

00:01:15.605 --> 00:01:18.724
data and repeated actions The goal is

00:01:18.737 --> 00:01:21.460
readable code not the most complicated code
